      "text": "Recall the general formula for calculating the modulus of a complex number.$|a+bi| = \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}$.\n   \nIf  $|{-4+ti}| = 2\\sqrt{13}$,\nwe have that,\n$ \\sqrt{(-4)^2 + t^2} = 2 \\sqrt{13} $,\nsolving for $t$,\n$ t^2 = 36 $,\nand therefore,\n$ t = \\pm 6$.\nWe eliminate the negative solution.\nThus, the answer is $\\boxed{6}$.",
